    <unit id="title">
      <segment>
        <source>Agentation</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="short_description">
      <segment>
        <source>Visual annotations for AI coding agents</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="description">
      <segment>
        <source>Connect a coding agent to the Agentation toolbar, check that the toolbar can run, and clean up stored annotations.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="module.heading">
      <segment>
        <source>Agentation</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="module.intro">
      <segment>
        <source>Backend users mark up frontend pages and backend screens with the Agentation toolbar; your coding agent receives each annotation, with selector, page and computed styles, through MCP.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.heading">
      <segment>
        <source>Connect your coding agent</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.intro">
      <segment>
        <source>Register the agentation-mcp server with your coding agent. It collects what the toolbar sends and hands it to the agent.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.localMode.title">
      <segment>
        <source>Local mode</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.localMode.text">
      <segment>
        <source>Annotations sync through an agentation-mcp server on the developer's computer (http://localhost:4747), which your agent starts. For the Agentation cloud, set an API key in the extension configuration.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.cloudMode.title">
      <segment>
        <source>Cloud mode</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.cloudMode.text">
      <segment>
        <source>Annotations are stored in the Agentation cloud with the API key from the extension configuration. The key stays on the server and in the configuration below.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.json.label">
      <segment>
        <source>MCP server configuration</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.json.hint">
      <segment>
        <source>For .mcp.json, Cursor, Windsurf, Zed or Continue.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.json.copy">
      <segment>
        <source>Copy configuration</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.addToCursor">
      <segment>
        <source>Add to Cursor</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.claude.label">
      <segment>
        <source>Claude Code</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.claude.hint">
      <segment>
        <source>Run this in a terminal where the claude command is installed.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="connect.claude.copy">
